From 225231378741cd3ded7132778b2cde90633e1698 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florent Kermarrec <florent@enjoy-digital.fr>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:03:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] board: use the CPU address for private WR diagnostics

The generated CPU device map places WDIAG at DEV_BASE + 0x800.
The previous 0x900 offset belongs to the host map and leaves the real
diagnostic RAM uninitialized. Use the CPU offset for BASE_WDIAGS_PRIV.

Validated on uRV firmware in LiteX-WR-NIC: host diagnostic version is 2
and live time, link, PTP and servo fields update on Acorn and SPEC-A7.
---
 include/board.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/board.h b/include/board.h
index a15fa2a1..0558cf61 100644
--- a/include/board.h
+++ b/include/board.h
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
 #define BASE_VUART              (DEV_BASE + 0x580)
 #define BASE_ONEWIRE            (DEV_BASE + 0x600)
 #define BASE_TIMECODE           (DEV_BASE + 0x700)
-#define BASE_WDIAGS_PRIV        (DEV_BASE + 0x900)
+#define BASE_WDIAGS_PRIV        (DEV_BASE + 0x800)
 #define BASE_CLOCK_MONITOR      (DEV_BASE + 0xa00)
 #ifndef BASE_AUXWB
 #define BASE_AUXWB              (DEV_BASE + 0x8000)
-- 
2.53.0

